\section{Hierarchical Composition of TSSE Kernels}

TSSE defines three primary kernel classes:
\[
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE}} =
\left\{
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-T}},\;
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-RPK}},\;
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-FK}}
\right\},
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-T}}$ is the Temporal Symmetry Kernel.
  \item $\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-RPK}}$ is the Relativistic Propulsion Kernel.
  \item $\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-FK}}$ is the Fusion Energetics Kernel.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Kernel Composition Rule}

\begin{definition}[TSSE Kernel Composition]
The TSSE kernel composition operator $\otimes$ satisfies:
\[
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE}} = 
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-T}}
\otimes
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-RPK}}
\otimes
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-FK}}.
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Associativity of Kernel Composition]
TSSE kernel composition is associative:
\[
(\mathcal{K}_A \otimes \mathcal{K}_B) \otimes \mathcal{K}_C
=
\mathcal{K}_A \otimes (\mathcal{K}_B \otimes \mathcal{K}_C).
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Each kernel is defined by a Hamiltonian, a temporal operator, and a structural
manifold. Composition corresponds to direct sum of Hamiltonians and direct product
of manifolds, both of which are associative.
\end{proof}

This establishes the hierarchical structure of TSSE engines.

