\section{Structural Manifold Topology}

Let $\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}}$ denote the global structural manifold of the engine:
\[
\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}} =
\mathcal{S}_{\text{T}}
\times
\mathcal{S}_{\text{RPK}}
\times
\mathcal{S}_{\text{FK}},
\]
where each component manifold is defined in Chapters 1–3.

\begin{definition}[TSSE Structural Manifold]
The TSSE structural manifold is the direct product of all subsystem manifolds:
\[
\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}} = 
\prod_{i=1}^3 \mathcal{S}_i.
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Manifold Closure]
If each $\mathcal{S}_i$ is closed under its subsystem evolution, then:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}} = \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}}.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since $\mathcal{U}(t)$ acts independently on each subsystem manifold and each
manifold is closed, the direct product is closed.
\end{proof}

This lemma ensures global structural stability of TSSE engines.

