\section{Hamiltonian Layering}

The TSSE engine Hamiltonian is:
\[
H_{\text{TSSE}} =
H_{\text{T}}
+
H_{\text{RPK}}
+
H_{\text{FK}},
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $H_{\text{T}}$ enforces temporal symmetry.
  \item $H_{\text{RPK}}$ governs relativistic propulsion.
  \item $H_{\text{FK}}$ governs fusion energetics.
\end{itemize}

\begin{lemma}[Hamiltonian Additivity]
TSSE Hamiltonians combine linearly:
\[
H_{\text{TSSE}} = \sum_{i=1}^3 H_i.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Each subsystem Hamiltonian acts on disjoint canonical coordinates. Therefore,
their sum is a valid Hamiltonian for the combined system.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[TSSE Hamiltonian Admissibility]
If each $H_i$ is TSSE-admissible, then $H_{\text{TSSE}}$ is TSSE-admissible.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Admissibility requires commutation with $\mathcal{T}$, symplectic evolution, and
manifold closure. Each property is preserved under Hamiltonian addition.
\end{proof}

This theorem establishes the Hamiltonian foundation of TSSE engines.

