\section{Canonical TSSE Engine Stack (TSSE-ES)}

The TSSE Engine Stack is defined by:
\[
\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}} =
\left(
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-T}},\;
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-RPK}},\;
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-FK}},\;
H_{\text{TSSE}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}},\;
\mathcal{T},\;
\mathcal{U}(t)
\right).
\]

It enforces:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}(t) = J,
\qquad
\mathcal{T}\mathcal{U}(t) = \mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{T},
\qquad
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}} = \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}}.
\]

This stack defines the complete TSSE system architecture.

